{
  "lesson_id": "b1_clauses_contrast_purpose_reason",
  "level": "B1",
  "title": "Clauses of contrast, purpose and reason",
  "description": "Clauses of contrast, purpose and reason отвечают на разные вопросы: несмотря на что? зачем? почему?",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-B1-32-RU",
    "lesson_num": 32,
    "title": "Правила: Clauses of contrast, purpose and reason",
    "level": "B1",
    "overview": "Clauses of contrast, purpose and reason отвечают на разные вопросы: несмотря на что? зачем? почему?",
    "main_rule": "Although/even though показывают unexpected contrast. To/in order to/so that выражают purpose. Because/since/as вводят reason.",
    "form": "although/even though + clause. to/in order to + V1. so that + clause. because/since/as + clause.",
    "when_why": "Сравни goal и cause: We left early to avoid traffic. / We changed the plan because the weather was bad.",
    "examples": "Although it was late, we continued. → Хотя было поздно, мы продолжили.\nWe left early to avoid traffic. → Мы ушли рано, чтобы избежать пробок.\nWe changed the plan because the weather was bad. → Мы изменили план, потому что погода была плохой.",
    "special_cases": "Purpose и reason не одно и то же: purpose = goal; reason = cause.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ We left early because catch the train. → ✅ We left early to catch the train.\n❌ We left early to the weather was bad. → ✅ We left early because the weather was bad.",
    "dont_confuse": "Спроси: what was the goal? → purpose. Why did it happen? → reason. Unexpected contrast? → although/even though.",
    "quick_summary": "contrast = although/even though.\npurpose = to/in order to/so that.\nreason = because/since/as."
  },
